#---
# purpose: "A list given to OtpJSON.encode_binary/1, whose spec says binary(), is refused at compile time"
# expect: diagnostic
# diagnostic.code: spec/violation
#---
# OTP's json.erl treats the spec as advisory: on the BEAM the call compiles and
# fails with function_clause at run time. fz refuses the call at compile time.
# The module holds the port's encode_binary/1 with its spec, guard and clause
# head, and a trimmed body; fixtures/01860 holds the whole port.
defmodule OtpJSON do
  @spec encode_binary(binary()) :: iodata()
  def encode_binary(bin) when is_binary(bin), do: [?", bin, ?"]
end

defmodule Main do
  def main() do
    IO.inspect(OtpJSON.encode_binary([1, 2, 3]))
  end
end

Main.main()
